// Ch13 B08 "Day two: the roll" (P → C, 4 min). act2_ch13.md §2 B08. R03: the Cantor roll, sixty-one names,
// and a column the public copies leave out: kept or spent. Seven are kept. R04: Corran's line, and the margin
// in a hand Ysolde has seen on every Warden's seal all her life. R05: Ysolde does the maths ON CORRAN HERE
// (ADR 0016 (b)), quietly and exactly. R06: hands flat on the lectern; Liss stands shoulder to shoulder with
// her and says nothing. RULE 1: nobody says "revenant".
title: ch13_archive_roll
location: ch13/lamp_archive
---
@camera R03
@music lamp_archive fade=1.0
Cantor roll. Sixtieth: Corran Ysel. Tender, Ansedra. Kept, Sanctum. #line:ch13_rec_roll_001 #narration #tn:"An entry in the Order's private Cantor roll. 'Kept' and 'Spent' are the hidden column's two values."
@camera R04
In the margin, small: to be spent at the next Calm. #line:ch13_rec_roll_002 #narration #tn:"A marginal note in a different, official hand: Ysolde recognises it from the Wardens' seals."
@camera R05
@music silence fade=2.0
Ysolde [cold]: Kept, Sanctum. To be spent at the next Calm. #line:ch13_roll_001
@wait 2.0
Ysolde [cold]: The next Calm is hers. #line:ch13_roll_002
@anim ysolde look_at asha
Ysolde [grief]: When you sing, Lady Cantor, they spend him. #line:ch13_roll_003
Asha [grief]: ...I have him. He's with me now. #line:ch13_roll_004
Ysolde [tender]: Then I would ask you to keep him a little longer. #line:ch13_roll_005
@camera R06
@anim ysolde hands_on_lectern
@mark liss beside_ysolde walk
@wait 5.0
<<set $ch13_read_cantor_roll = true>>
@camera release
===
